{
  "abstract": "We develop collective bounds for original selected quadratic jet columns in the explicit tenth-discriminant framework. A positive completion of the physical Charlier kernel factors into Bargmann–Fock and Hardy components. Normalizing the original selected blocks preserves nonprefix selections and all global omissions. A Laguerre generating bound first gives a closed cumulative rectangular spectrum. A constructive refinement dominates the finite Fock jet projector by a coherent-state disk with polynomial cost, then identifies each positive charge as a factorial contraction of a Hardy kernel. Finite Blaschke model spaces retain the linked displacement geometry; an explicit boundary reduction and directed interval certificate cover a fixed rational band table uniformly. At the unchanged accepted $D=347$ source contract, the replacement metric correction exceeds 0.0019260307467869571 and the complete imported-source gap exceeds 0.0415357741976371247. An integer-scale argument retains a correction above 0.0019260304799624727 under the same normalized geometry and original-selection hypotheses. An independent public audit covers the coherent-disk proof and fixed consumer with a slightly weaker outward enclosure; the sharper endpoints, cumulative refinements and integer-scale theorem retain author-proof status. The scaling theorem is metric only and supplies no scaled arithmetic rank certificates or complete scaled contradictions. Classical ingredients and earlier audits are credited separately. No new endpoint, census or classification is claimed. The imported $D\\le498$ consequence retains its separate $D\\le499$ theorem qualification. Reproduction includes exact controls, the uniform geometric enclosure and all source-cost and omission debits.",
